\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Weary of earth and laden with my sin,
\par I look at heaven and long to enter in;
\par But there no evil thing may find a home,
\par And yet I hear a voice that bids me: Come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. So vile I am, how dare I hope to stand
\par In the pure glory of that holy land,
\par Before the whiteness of that throne appear?
\par Yet there are hands stretched 
\par out to draw me near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 3. The while I fain would tread the 
\par heavenly way,
\par Evil is ever with me day by day;
\par Yet on mine ears the gracious tidings fall:
\par Repent, believe; thou shalt be 
\par loosed from all!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. It is the voice of Jesus that I hear,
\par His are the hands stretched out to
\par draw me near,
\par And His the blood that can for all atone,
\par And set me faultless there before 
\par the throne.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. 'Twas He who found me on the
\par deathly wild,
\par And made me heir of heaven, the 
\par Father's child,
\par And day by day, whereby my soul
\par may live,
\par Gives me His grace of pardon,
\par and will give.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O great Absolver, grant my soul
\par may wear
\par The lowliest garb of penitence and prayer,
\par That in the Father's courts my 
\par glorious dress
\par May be the garment of Thy righteousness.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Yea, Thou wilt answer for me,
\par righteous Lord:
\par Thine all the merits, mine the great
\par reward;
\par Thine the sharp thorns, and mine
\par the golden crown;
\par Mine the life won, and Thine the 
\par life laid down.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Nought can I bring Thee, Lord,
\par for all I owe;
\par Yet let my full heart what it can
\par bestow:
\par Like Mary's gift, let my devotion prove,
\par Forgiven greatly, how I greatly love.
\par                                                  Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

